// The executable's own icon - what Explorer, the taskbar's pinned entry and
// the Alt+Tab switcher read off the binary, none of which run any of our code
// and so none of which can see QApplication::setWindowIcon().
//
// CONFIGURED, not compiled as-is: rc.exe resolves a relative path against its
// own working directory and its include path, neither of which is reliably the
// source tree under a multi-config generator. CMake substitutes an absolute
// path here (forward slashes, which rc accepts), so the reference cannot break
// depending on where the build ran from.
//
// IDI_ICON1 is a plain string name rather than a defined identifier, which is
// what Qt's own documentation uses: Windows shows the icon whose name sorts
// first, and this is the only one in the binary.
IDI_ICON1 ICON "@FURNIFYME_ICON_FILE@"
